      "writtenOn": "2023-01-23T17:38:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Fan vendor has decided min \u0026 max rpm \u0026 fanduty %  based on their testing and has noted in cross bug. Also, I didnot find it correct to derive fanduty cycle from the given rpm min \u0026 max for brya. For instance, if we take rpm max of 4200 as 100 % duty cycle, rpm for 30% duty cycle must have been ideally 1260, which is not matching the minimum rpm configured in brya (2200). I think, there is some marginal value which gets added  to the rpm that varies for different fans, which means, we cannot derive fanduty directly from these values.",
      "parentUuid": "2f1d74fc_cb6cc118",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2046,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2047,
        "endChar": 35
