      "writtenOn": "2023-01-30T16:48:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Dai,\n30% duty  is defined in fan spec definition(Also compal has confirmed same in comment#6 in cross bug)(spec says- Fan will be able to start when the duty cycle is 30%.)\nIn the fan spec , it is defined as when duty \u003d 100%, fan rpm \u003d \n3800 +- 7% , which also doesn\u0027t seem to the spec truely because below is my observation:\nWhen duty is increased to 30%, rpm \u003d ~1923(say, prev duty was 12 to 30 ). If reduced from higher to lower duty as 30%, rpm \u003d ~ 2300.  similary , when duty \u003d 100, rpm \u003d ~ 4866.  I think the error margin changes for diff fan types.",
      "parentUuid": "4e8aee59_f0e97477",
